\f3\fs26 Shakti found himself standing tall before the man, wondering what he had done this time. He had received genuine congratulations for his thorough investigation into Director\'85\'85 murder, so it couldn\'92t be that could it? All the information pointed to a random murder-suicide, but Shakti was convinced there was a conspiracy at play. 
\f4\i I\'92ve looked under every crook and nanny, haven\'92t I? No arrests so far, but I\'92ll get there.
\f3\i0 \
\'93I have it on good authority, Lieutenant, that you faked the recording on the Hammersmith case! You are in big trouble Shakti.\'94 The Commissioner was yelling and screaming, but his heart wasn\'92t in it. He knew there was not much he could do to Shakti without upsetting his mother and no-one wanted to make her unhappy. Her tendrils reached everywhere.\
\'93I don\'92t know what you mean.\'94 Wiley old colleagues had once told him never admit anything. The cops age old adage - 
\f4\i They can charge me with breathing and I\'92ll plead not guilty, 
\f3\i0 was repeating itself in his mind and he would hold out no matter how long it took.\
\'93Look Shakti, I know you did it and you know you did it. I don\'92t care about some L.2 you loaded-up. I want you to do me a favour.\'94\
\'93Okay. I will do it.\'94 Shakti capitulated. He had held out for all of three seconds.\
\'93I want you to be the lead officer in the arrest of the Nightclub Vampire. We have only just identified him and you have to act fast or he might get away. The files are on this stick. Get an arrest team together and move!\'94\
\'93Yes, sir.\'94 Shakti thought he was going to be punished but this arrest would really give him the credibility he desired. This serial killer had been operating with impunity for years and his apprehension had become even more urgent in recent times when a couple of L.5. girls became victims. \
\'93Do not fuck this up.\'94 He said those precise words so often, the Commissioner reflected, it could be his epitaph. He was perfectly aware that Shakti would make a meal of this arrest, but it didn\'92t matter. He had already offered a bounty on the head of the suspect, a promotion for the man or woman who disposes of him. The Nightclub Vampire would be dead before morning.\
Returning to his office, Shakti was shocked to see the name of the one suspect when he opened the file. Anthony Hardy, Cleaner L.2, his only friend in the world, was a serial killer. He was hurt profoundly and deeply, but only allowed a few tears to escape before taking some solace in the knowledge that having no friends meant there was no one left to betray him. It appears, he thought, that the old clich\'e9 is true, friends do always shit on you. \
\'93No one can hurt you now.\'94 He steeled himself for the task ahead, arresting and charging his ex-best friend with a capital offence. He studied the contents of the file as best he could, but found it far too complicated and decided to trust the Commissioner on this one. The evidence, he thought, had to be solid, didn\'92t it?\
Shakti and the arrest team approached the entrance of the teetering, rusted iron and concrete structure, forensic teams and tactical support in the rear waiting for the all clear. There was a member of the public, a man dressed in a black suit, in the foetal position on the concrete just adjacent to the entrance, crying like a baby. After some considerable time one of the arrest team approached him and gave him a good kick and told him to fuck off. Agent Jones scuttled off, sobbing and howling. At the moment he was to give the team the go order, Shakti saw two women emerge from the entrance. He recognised one as the much lauded Detective Supt Hayley Lanning, but at a distance he was unable to recognise the blonde. He sent in the team as soon as the ladies were clear of the access point. He waved them over as his men stormed the building.\
Detective Lanning stomped over to Shakti leaving Sarah trailing in her wake, \'93What is going Lieutenant? What is the meaning of this?\'94\
\'93The Commissioner selected me to lead the team to arrest the Nightclub Vampire.\'94 \
\'93That\'92s my brief! Who is your suspect?\'94 Hayley could not believe the Commissioner would hand such a sensitive matter over to this fool. \'93Answer me!\'94\
Sarah had caught up and Shakti finally got a good look at her. \'93Dream woman!\'94 Shakti blurted out and stumbled back several steps. His stomach was churning and his body shaking noticeably as his system flooded with adrenaline, reacting to the deep shock of literally meeting the woman of his dreams. All sorts of liquids wanted to squirt out the nearest orifice as he tried desperately not to piss, shit or vomit.\
\'93Dream woman? Is that a nick-name for the perp?\'94\
\'93No, sorry. His name is Anthony Hardy, Cleaner, L.2.\'94\
\'93You are kidding. We were just speaking to him about another Commissioner\'92s special investigation. He seems harmless. I trust your evidence is solid.\'94\
\'93The Commissioner said it was.\'94\
\'93You had better hope he is right.\'94 She knew the brief back to front. Forensics and physical evidence were almost non-existent. She wondered what breakthroughs had been made in her absence and lamented being dragged away by the Commissioner to find a missing labourer. \
\'93What\'92s all the fuss, Detective?\'94 Sarah caught some of the conversation and urgently wanted to fill in the blanks. \
\'93Lieutenant Shakti, this is a Sarah Jacobson, Ph.D. L.5. Sarah this is Lieutenant Shakti, L.5.\'94 Hayley decided introductions were the first order of business, deliberately highlighting Shakti\'92s lack of tertiary qualifications. It was rumoured that he didn\'92t even get through high school, but all those records were unavailable to the public thanks to intervention from his mother.\
\'93Lieutenant, pleased to meet you. I have heard so much about you.\'94 Anyone within hearing immediately began to giggling. He wasn\'92t famous for his professionalism.\
\'93Please, call me Alex. No rank.\'94 He hoped she was not in the public service. His mother would not like that.\
\'93I\'92m a privateer on a long term contract.\'94 Sarah was also keen to distance herself from the public service.\
\'93Alex here is in the process of arresting the Nightclub Vampire, Anthony Hardy. On Commissioner\'92s instructions no less.\'94 Hayley thought to bring Sarah up to speed.\
\'93What? He\'92s harm\'85., he seems harmless. Theft I would believe, but multiple murders?\'94 Sarah was exasperated. What had Cracker been up to in his spare time? As she let her thoughts settle, a loud 
\f4\i \'93All Clear, suspect in custody\'94
\f3\i0  crackled over the air. The support crews grabbed the equipment and headed inside and up the stairs. \
\'93Do you mind if I tag along, Alex?\'94 Hayley was going in no matter what, but thought she should try diplomacy as a first port of call. \'93Sarah you go back to the office and have this Disc checked out. Try our tech-teams first, but I think this thing will be military hardware and way out of their league. Perhaps you can wrangle an expert from your contacts in the cyber-security universe. It seems to be right up your alley, actually.\'94\
\'93Can you put it in an evidence bag, Lieutenant?\'94 Sarah was not keen for her skin to touch another one of these wretched discs.\
\'93Yes, yes. Anything.\'94 He grabbed an evidence bag from the forensics truck and returned smiling wide, mission accomplished. \'93Well I will be off then. Nice to meet you Lieutenant.\'94
